.TH TRILL 1 "2026-11-19" "trill 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trill \- control the Trill daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trill
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trill
is the command-line control tool for \fBtrilld\fR, a daemon that streams
system audio to Android devices using Roc and PipeWire.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON output on stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-socket " \fIPATH\fR"
Override the daemon IPC socket path. Defaults to \fI$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/trill/ctl.sock\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B pair [\-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR]
Open a pairing window and display the 6-digit SPAKE2 pairing code.
.TP
.B list
List paired devices and their connection status.
.TP
.B status
Display daemon status, active sink, connected sessions, and streaming metrics.
.TP
.B start \fIDEVICE\fR
Ask a connected phone to begin streaming audio.
.TP
.B stop [\fIDEVICE\fR]
Stop streaming for a specific device, or stop all streams if no device is given.
.TP
.B unpair \fIDEVICE\fR
Remove the pairing certificate pin and drop any active session for the device.
.TP
.B rename \fIDEVICE\fR \fINAME\fR
Assign a human-readable label to a paired device.
.TP
.B shutdown
Gracefully terminate the \fBtrilld\fR daemon.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operation failed (connection error, timeout, rejected request).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/trill/config.toml
Server configuration file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/trill/devices.json
Known paired devices and pinned certificates.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/trill/ctl.sock
UNIX domain socket for local IPC.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/trill/trilld.log
Daemon log file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pipewire (1),
.BR pw-cli (1)
